  "findings": [
    "The three years reconcile to 180 EC, with 55/95/30 core/major/minor. The Free Major preserves the target’s disciplinary breadth. The 15 EC thesis is part of the 25 EC third-year major; first opportunity is semester six for a September entrant. Two complete years supply the required first-year and later credit thresholds; approval of the programme is also required.",
    "The broad option connects environmental science and governance to liberal arts breadth and research, while the second concentrates on molecular, neural and behavioural accounts of health. The third applies economics and law to institutions and businesses. It supplies firm-level practice and cross-border law while leaving international operations and specialist management depth limited.",
    "Psycholinguistics precedes later neuroscience in its supported first-year spring term and follows the gateway. Advanced psychology research is systematic evidence synthesis, not an annual group project equivalent. The UCR optional independent research row is separate from the compulsory Groningen thesis and adds no UCR schedule credits."
  ],
